---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<Legal
  title="Treatment Consent | The Better Face"
  description="What informed consent means at The Better Face: what you will be told before a treatment, what you are agreeing to, and your right to change your mind."
  path="/consent/"
  heading="Treatment consent"
  updated="TODO — date of counsel sign-off"
>
  <p>
    This page explains, in advance, what you will be asked to consent to. It is
    published so that nothing at your appointment is a surprise. The document you
    sign in clinic is the operative one.
  </p>

  <h2>Informed consent</h2>
  <p>Before any treatment, your practitioner will explain, and you will have the chance to ask about:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>What the treatment does and how it works.</li>
    <li>What outcome is realistic for <em>your</em> skin, and over what timescale.</li>
    <li>The expected number of sessions and the total cost.</li>
    <li>Side effects that are expected, and complications that are possible but rare.</li>
    <li>The alternatives, including doing nothing.</li>
    <li>What aftercare is required, and what happens to the result if it is not followed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You are consenting to a specific treatment on a specific date. Consent to one
    session is not consent to a course.
  </p>

  <h2>You can change your mind</h2>
  <p>
    You may withdraw consent at any point, including after a treatment has begun,
    and we will stop. <strong>TODO — state how this affects fees already paid.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Photography</h2>
  <p>
    Clinical photographs are taken as part of your record so that change can be
    assessed objectively. That is separate from permission to publish. We will
    never use your image in marketing, on this website or on social media without
    specific written consent, given separately, which you can revoke at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Medical history</h2>
  <p>
    You are asked to disclose medications, conditions, allergies, prior treatments
    and whether you are pregnant or breastfeeding. Some of our treatments are
    unsafe in those circumstances, so an incomplete history is a safety risk rather
    than a formality.
  </p>

  <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Contact the clinic immediately on {site.phoneDisplay}. Complications are
    uncommon and most resolve quickly when treated early.
    <strong> TODO — add out-of-hours contact arrangements.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Ask before you sign, not after: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
